+
+## Pending configuration compare-and-set correction
+
+The pending SQL configuration command now takes optional `p_expected_revision`.
+Five-argument callers can still create a pool and retry the exact same policy.
+They cannot change an existing revision. A six-argument update requires the
+expected previous revision under the row lock and refuses while reservations
+are held. An expected revision never creates an absent pool. Exact same-policy
+retries acknowledge the current row without resetting or refreshing its reading,
+even after the original transition succeeded but its reply was lost.
+
+A caller must not turn a timeout into a fresh unconditional write or silently
+replace its expected revision with the latest one. Read back exact host, pool,
+revision, capacity and freshness policy; compare observation and timestamp
+separately. A true configuration result does not prove a fresh observation or
+admission eligibility. Revision IDs identify immutable policy contents and must
+not be reused for a different policy; this CAS is not a numeric revision ordering,
+a writer lease, cross-host authentication or a new permission grant.
+
+The prepared SQL regression includes a five-argument stale-writer assertion that
+fails on the original function, concurrent create/update contenders, an absent-pool
+CAS, invalid expected revision, exact same-policy readback, retained stale reading,
+old-revision observation refusal and held-policy refusal with a valid expectation.
+Client role denials cover both call arities. **Correction SQL execution: NOT_RUN**
+until the integration owner provides the serialized disposable database slot.
+No active migration manifest, service configuration or portable protocol changes.
